88 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (This project proposes an IoT-based Pothole Detection System designed for real-time monitoring and alerting of road potholes. Employing two ultrasonic sensors and GPS technology, the system ensures accurate detection and precise location tracking. Alerts are relayed to drivers through a mobile app using a buzzer and handle vibrator. Additionally, the integration of the ESP32-CAM module allows for the capture of pothole images, which are transmitted to a Telegram channel along with GPS and ultrasonic data. The algorithm for pothole detection operates in real-time, and recorded data can be accessed by authorized individuals and drivers through a dedicated app or webpage. This system offers a comprehensive approach to road safety and maintenance, enhancing driver awareness and facilitating timely interventions. )
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
89 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 62 0 R
/E (      Potholes on roads pose significant risks to drivers and pedestrians, leading to accidents, vehicle damage, and traffic congestion. This report presents an IoT-based system designed for real-time detection and alert generation for potholes. The system leverages various sensors \(e.g., accelerometers, GPS\) integrated with a microcontroller to identify road irregularities. Data collected from these sensors is transmitted wirelessly to a cloud platform for processing and analysis. Upon detecting a pothole, the system automatically generates alerts, which can be disseminated to relevant authorities and road users via SMS, email, or a dedicated mobile application. This proactive approach aims to facilitate timely road maintenance, enhance road safety, and improve overall traffic management. The proposed system offers a cost-effective and efficient solution for infrastructure monitoring, contributing to smarter city initiatives and safer travel experiences.)
/Pg 10 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
