103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 66 0 R
/E (The primary problem addressed by this project is the lack of an efficient and immediate system for identifying and reporting road potholes. Current methods are often reactive, addressing potholes only after they have caused significant issues or been manually reported. This delay leads to prolonged periods of hazardous road conditions, contributing to accidents, increasing vehicle maintenance costs for citizens, and hindering effective road management by authorities. There is a clear need for an automated, proactive system that can detect potholes in real-time, pinpoint their exact locations, and promptly notify the relevant maintenance departments and public users.)
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
