/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 68 0 R
/E (The proposed system employs a multi-sensor approach. An accelerometer \(e.g., MPU6050\) measures vibrations and sudden jolts experienced by the vehicle, indicating changes in road surface. A GPS module \(e.g., NEO-6M\) provides precise location coordinates. A microcontroller \(e.g., ESP32\) collects data from these sensors, processes it, and transmits it wirelessly via Wi-Fi to a cloud-based platform \(e.g., Thingspeak, AWS IoT\). The processing algorithm analyzes accelerometer data for abnormal peaks and uses a thresholding technique to differentiate potholes from minor bumps. Once a pothole is confirmed, its GPS coordinates are packaged with a timestamp and sent to the cloud. The cloud platform then triggers alerts \(e.g., SMS, email\) to predefined recipients, such as municipal road maintenance departments and navigation apps.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
113 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 68 0 R
/T (5. Methodology/Procedure)
/E (5. Methodology/Procedure)
/Pg 16 0 R
