endobj
114 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 69 0 R
/T (6. Results and Discussion The implemented prototype system demonstrated promising results in detecting potholes under various road conditions. Field tests conducted on local roads showed a high accuracy rate in identifying potholes, with precise location tracking. The accelerometer data, when filtered and processed, effectively distinguished between normal road vibrations and significant impacts caused by potholes. The wireless data transmission to the cloud was reliable, and alerts were generated promptly. Challenges included optimizing sensor sensitivity to reduce false positives from speed bumps or minor undulations, and ensuring stable GPS signal acquisition in all environments. Future enhancements will focus on machine learning algorithms for improved classification and predictive maintenance.)
/E (6. Results and Discussion The implemented prototype system demonstrated promising results in detecting potholes under various road conditions. Field tests conducted on local roads showed a high accuracy rate in identifying potholes, with precise location tracking. The accelerometer data, when filtered and processed, effectively distinguished between normal road vibrations and significant impacts caused by potholes. The wireless data transmission to the cloud was reliable, and alerts were generated promptly. Challenges included optimizing sensor sensitivity to reduce false positives from speed bumps or minor undulations, and ensuring stable GPS signal acquisition in all environments. Future enhancements will focus on machine learning algorithms for improved classification and predictive maintenance.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
115 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 70 0 R
/T (7. Conclusion and Future Scope This IoT-based pothole detection and alert system offers an effective and automated solution to a pervasive urban problem. By leveraging low-cost sensors and cloud connectivity, the system provides real-time detection, precise localization, and immediate notification, significantly improving road safety and maintenance efficiency. The proactive nature of the system ensures that potholes can be addressed before they lead to serious incidents.)
/E (7. Conclusion and Future Scope This IoT-based pothole detection and alert system offers an effective and automated solution to a pervasive urban problem. By leveraging low-cost sensors and cloud connectivity, the system provides real-time detection, precise localization, and immediate notification, significantly improving road safety and maintenance efficiency. The proactive nature of the system ensures that potholes can be addressed before they lead to serious incidents.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [0]
>>
endobj
116 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/P 70 0 R
/T (Future scope includes integrating additional sensors \(e.g., depth sensors, cameras for visual confirmation\), developing a comprehensive mobile application for public reporting and viewing of pothole maps, and deploying a network of such devices on public transport for continuous monitoring. Further research can explore integration with smart city infrastructure and traffic management systems for more holistic road condition monitoring.)
/E (Future scope includes integrating additional sensors \(e.g., depth sensors, cameras for visual confirmation\), developing a comprehensive mobile application for public reporting and viewing of pothole maps, and deploying a network of such devices on public transport for continuous monitoring. Further research can explore integration with smart city infrastructure and traffic management systems for more holistic road condition monitoring.)
/Pg 18 0 R
/K [1]
>>
