277 0 obj
<<
/Title (6. Results and Discussion The implemented prototype system demonstrated promising results in detecting potholes under various road conditions. Field tests conducted on local roads showed a high accuracy rate in identifying potholes, with precise location tracking. The accelerometer data, when filtered and processed, effectively distinguished between normal road vibrations and significant impacts caused by potholes. The wireless data transmission to the cloud was reliable, and alerts were generated promptly. Challenges included optimizing sensor sensitivity to reduce false positives from speed bumps or minor undulations, and ensuring stable GPS signal acquisition in all environments. Future enhancements will focus on machine learning algorithms for improved classification and predictive maintenance.)
/Dest [17 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 329 0 R
/Next 221 0 R
>>
