355 0 obj
<<
/Title (2. Background                 Previous research and existing solutions for road anomaly detection often rely on image processing, vibration analysis, or a combination thereof. Image-based systems typically involve mounting cameras on vehicles, capturing road images, and using computer vision algorithms to identify potholes. While effective, these systems can be computationally intensive and sensitive to lighting conditions. Vibration- based systems, on the other hand, use accelerometers to measure vehicle vibrations, correlating unusual patterns with road defects. The integration of GPS allows for the precise localization of detected anomalies. Our system builds upon these principles by leveraging the ubiquity of IoT devices to provide a scalable, real-time, and location-aware solution.)
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 328 0 R
/Next 357 0 R
>>
endobj
